title the adoption completes, and the stars run once on any power
prompt kg, with two words mid-flight: a run-once command in all three star launchers, and the loops riding battery and outage -- the mesh over any one node.
think The round opened into the peer's staged repair and carried it home first (%291, the commit before this one). Then Mind's runner refused print with UndefinedName, and the trail led somewhere better than a fix: the run-bounded builtin its run-bounded calls need was never in this checkout's rishi -- my earlier adoption grepped the branch diff for mind and arbor and silently dropped every other room the branch carried. The completion adopts thirty-seven more files from keep-arbor-voice-prekiln: the rishi bounded-process round (the run-bounded builtin in rishi/src/main.rye, thirteen tests, the control fixture, both language references), the alias-sameness rule pair with its scan and control, Mind's Skate native core (the Swift package, EventRing and FrameGrid, tests, witness), the codex research note, and the gitignore and manifest rows for the skate room. rishi rebuilt; the probe answers ok=true and refuses an absolute output path by its own ProcessPathUnsafe wall; Mind's print mode speaks its whole seat.
think The alias-sameness scan then redded my own tree -- five faults, all Surf-versus-Skate asymmetry -- and the branch's fix could not be taken whole because its LEXICON carries the cross-rewrite over-swaps %290 named. The one good hunk lifted alone: the Surf / Skate peer row seated in the LEXICON, the three-stars lane worded as peers, zero faults after, and the Skate native-core witness GREEN on metal -- Surf and Skate share one Frame and event-ring identity by compile-time alias.
think The launchers: Mind already carries once --arm-once in its printed handoff, so Sound and Dream gained a ONE ROUND section each, with the seat prompt hoisted into a single let both the once line and the loop line render -- one copy, no drift; a first render failed because the let sat below its first reader, and hoisting it above the once section taught the order plainly. Dream's prompt also dropped its two raw apostrophes, which would have broken the paste's own single quotes. The power word landed in all three: Mind's AC assert became a report, Sound's preconditions name adapter and caffeinate as preferred rather than required, Dream gained the survival paragraph -- the repo is the durable memory, a cut lap costs only its uncommitted work, the next round-open pull resumes the thread.
obs Two stamps in this sitting were written from memory before the clock was read -- the %282 closure clause the peer caught, and then the erratum correcting it, caught before commit. The erratum stands at the true reading and names both breaches; the lesson is now twice-taught: read the clock, then write.
